new file mode 100644
index 000000000..e78f1c95e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/doc/nng.md
@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
+# Optional NNG validation notifications (experimental)
+
+Configure with `-DBUILD_BITCOIN_NNG=ON` and install NNG development files
+(`find_package(nng CONFIG REQUIRED)`, tested NNG 1.12.4). The default is OFF;
+builds with NNG disabled do not find or link NNG. ZeroMQ is independent and
+unchanged. No mining, mempool policy, Chronik or consensus patch is required.
+
+Run with an explicit endpoint, for example:
+
+```
+bitcoind -nngpub=tcp://127.0.0.1:28335
+```
+
+No endpoint is opened unless requested. An invalid/busy endpoint fails node
+initialization. Use a local endpoint: this protocol has no authentication or
+confidentiality. Connect an NNG SUB socket and subscribe to topic prefixes with
+`NNG_OPT_SUB_SUBSCRIBE`. Notifications are best effort, including during initial
+block download; slow/absent subscribers do not block validation. Recover gaps
+with the ordinary node RPCs. The socket send buffer is configured to four messages. This bounds that
+queue's message count, not total transport memory or bytes (raw blocks may
+be large).
+
+Each NNG message is one frame:
+
+| Bytes | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| 0..11 | ASCII topic, padded with zero bytes to 12 bytes |
+| 12..19 | Little-endian uint64 sequence, shared across all topics |
+| 20..end | Payload below |
+
+| Topic | Payload |
+|---|---|
+| `updateblktip` | 32-byte new tip hash |
+| `mempooltxadd` | Raw network-serialized transaction |
+| `mempooltxrem` | 32-byte transaction ID |
+| `blkconnected` | Raw network-serialized block |
+| `blkdisconctd` | Raw network-serialized disconnected block |
+| `chainstflush` | 32-byte persisted tip hash |
+
+Hashes use network serialization order (reverse bytes for RPC hexadecimal).
+Sequences begin at zero on each process start, advance for every attempted
+notification and may have gaps. Subscribing to only some topics also produces
+gaps. A SUB client joining an existing publisher may first observe any value.
+BCHN does not emit `UpdatedBlockTip` for pure invalidation without a replacement
+branch; use disconnected block headers to follow that rollback.
+Connection events can precede a coalesced tip update; do not assume one tip
+notification per connected block. Blocks' transactions leave the mempool via
+`blkconnected`; conflicting transactions are notified as `mempooltxrem` before
+that event. Chainstate-flushed notifications establish persistence, as in the
+BCHN validation-interface contract.
+
+This is a **new BCHN raw-payload protocol**, inspired by Lotus's notification
+names. It is **not wire-compatible** with Lotus's 12-byte topic + FlatBuffers
+messages. It deliberately does not expose the older NNG request/reply service,
+spent-coin/undo offsets, metadata or FlatBuffers schema. A full Lotus protocol
+port would additionally need BCHN global chainstate/block-storage adaptation,
+spent-coin snapshots at admission, resource-limited read RPCs, and tests of
+undo positions and reorgs. Those are independent follow-up work, not implied
+by this publisher. Neither interface changes accepted blocks or transactions.
+
+Test with `test/functional/interface_nng.py --configfile=build/test/config.ini`.
+On systems where ctypes cannot locate Homebrew libraries, pass
+`--nng-library=/opt/homebrew/lib/libnng.dylib`. The test uses ctypes against the installed NNG shared library, checks real
+regtest raw block/hash and admitted transaction payloads, sequence order,
+mining inclusion, invalidation, failed-bind
+cleanup and restart. It skips when NNG is disabled or its test shared library
+is unavailable. This test does not measure throughput or establish indexer
+recovery, delivery guarantees or network security.
